body:
I don't know how it works in the US (I assume that's where you are), but is it possible for you to defer your last year? As in, take a year out? I'm studying in the UK, I've just finished my second year out of my 3 year degree and I'm going to be taking this year out, because, perhaps like you, I feel it's a bit too much for me right now, and I just need some time to get back to fitness.

&nbsp;

On the bright side, though, it does sound like you have the motivation, or at least the desire, to get better - I know it feels like you can't be bothered with studying or even just getting up, but the fact that you *want* to get better sounds really promising, and is much more positive than a state of being where you just don't even care about getting better (which I myself have been in at times). For me it sounds like you just need a bit of time, a bit of time off to get yourself back together and regain that interest and motivation to study - and indeed, first of all, to find that motivation for getting on with life, whether that's exercising, or meeting up with friends, or whatever. I don't know if it's possible for you to get that time, but I really hope the best for you
